{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_07_integrations_ports_and_adapters", "label": "Ports & Adapters (one interface, one adapter per environment)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Domain code never sees a port; orchestration calls the port and feeds results into pure domain functions, so swapping an adapter is a one-line provider change plus config."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_portresult", "label": "PortResult status envelope (never throw across a port)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ok / unavailable / unconfigured / error are distinct states so a missing key degrades gracefully instead of looking like an outage; HTTP relays return 200 with the envelope."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_withmetering", "label": "withMetering adapter wrapper", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Metering is a fire-and-forget enqueue so it never blocks or fails the request; billable metrics run the entitlement check BEFORE the call, non-billable ones are metered anyway for quotas and COGS dashboards."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_circuit_breaker", "label": "Circuit Breaker (5 failures \u2192 open 60s \u2192 half-open)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_solardataport", "label": "SolarDataPort (PVGIS \u2014 energy source of record)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PVGIS is the ONLY energy source and no adapter may introduce a second irradiance path without an ADR; unavailability falls back to a labelled estimate rather than blocking the design."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_buildinginsightsport", "label": "BuildingInsightsPort (Google Solar \u2014 enhancement, never dependency)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "India coverage is patchy, so no feature may depend on Google Solar existing; flux/irradiance layers are never requested."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_roofdetectport", "label": "RoofDetectPort (DSM primary, Gemini fallback)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both paths exit through validateArtifact \u2014 no AI output enters a Project any other way; Gemini runs at temperature 0 with an enforced response schema, a versioned prompt and no-guessing instructions because an empty result beats an invented roof."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_ssrf_guard", "label": "GeoTIFF relay SSRF guard (exact-prefix allowlist)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_telephonycoreport", "label": "TelephonyCorePort \u2014 capability-negotiated port family (ADR-0019)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Telephony is a platform capability, never one vendor-shaped interface: adapters declare what they truly support via getCapabilities() and business logic branches on the declaration, never on the vendor name."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_capability_degradation_ladder", "label": "Capability Degradation Ladder (binding)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A feature needing a missing capability degrades on a defined path \u2014 never throws, never silently no-ops: warm transfer falls to cold transfer plus push, IVR traversal without dtmfSend flags the call ivr_blocked for human follow-up."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_speechprovider", "label": "SpeechProvider + LanguageModel (Sarvam)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_compliancegate", "label": "ComplianceGate \u2014 ours, non-swappable", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TRAI penalties land on the tenant as Principal Entity, so the gate lives in our code rather than the vendor's; it fails closed \u2014 stale DND scrub pauses promotional dialing and there is no override flag."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_messagingport", "label": "MessagingPort (ManualCopyAdapter v1, BYO-WABA v2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rendering the message and letting the rep paste it carries zero regulatory surface and zero cost; in v2 each tenant owns their own WABA so deliverability reputation is isolated and assets survive a provider switch."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_paymentlinkport", "label": "PaymentLinkPort (BYO-Razorpay per tenant)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Funds settle customer \u2192 EPC's own merchant account, so the platform never touches funds and needs no RBI Payment Aggregator licence; Razorpay Route stays a documented alternate adapter only."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_subscriptionbillingport", "label": "SubscriptionBillingPort (Razorpay Subscriptions)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_documentrenderport", "label": "DocumentRenderPort (Playwright now, Typst swap)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The customer link always renders the proposal as web \u2014 the PDF is an artifact, never the only path to the number."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_pushport", "label": "PushPort (FCM HTTP v1 + APNs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Push is best-effort by contract; the notifications table is the source of truth, so a dropped push never loses information."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_otpport", "label": "OtpPort (MSG91 SMS \u2192 WhatsApp fallback)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No silent degradation on the front door: both channels failing means login fails loudly with an ops alert, because OTP delivery failure rate is an alerting metric."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_mapsport", "label": "MapsPort (server-fetched satellite tiles stored in Tigris)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fetching once per site capture gives stable 1:1 pixel mapping for detection, reproducible provenance (the tile a design was traced on never changes under it) and one billing event instead of per-render fetches."}, {"id": "docs_07_integrations_demport", "label": "DemPort (Copernicus GLO-30)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_07_integrations_ports_and_adapters", "target": "docs_07_integrations_portresult", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_07_integrations_ports_and_adapters", "target": "docs_07_integrations_withmetering", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_07_integrations_ports_and_adapters", "target": "docs_07_integrations_circuit_breaker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_07_integrations_solardataport", "target": "docs_07_integrations_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_07_integrations_buildinginsightsport", "target": "docs_07_integrations_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/07-integrations.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_07_integrations_roofdetectport", "target": "docs_07_integrations_por